## 6. Full-working example (copy-paste)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre Fly-to Demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@2.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <style>
    html,body{margin:0;height:100%;}
    #map{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;width:100%;}
    .control{
      position:absolute;top:10px;left:10px;
      background:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
      padding:8px 12px;border-radius:4px;
      font-family:sans-serif;cursor:pointer;
    }
    .sr-only{
      position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;
      overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<div class="control" id="flyBtn">✈️ Fly to Paris</div>
<p id="mapDesc" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite"></p>

<script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@2.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',
    center: [-0.1276, 51.5074],
    zoom: 10,
    pitch: 0,
    bearing: 0
  });

  function flyToLocation(lngLat, opts = {}) {
    const prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const base = {
      center: lngLat,
      zoom: 12,
      bearing: 0,
      pitch: 45,
      speed: 1.2,
      curve: 1.42,
      duration: 2000,
      essential: true
    };
    const flyOpts = Object.assign(base, opts);
    if (prefersReduced) map.jumpTo(flyOpts);
    else map.flyTo(flyOpts);
  }

  function updateMapDescription(lngLat, name) {
    const desc = `Map moved to ${name} (lon ${lngLat[0].toFixed(4)}, lat ${lngLat[1].toFixed(4)}).`;
    document.getElementById('mapDesc').textContent = desc;
  }

  document.getElementById('flyBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const paris = [2.2945, 48.8584];
    flyToLocation(paris, { zoom: 14, pitch: 60, bearing: 30, duration: 2500 });
    updateMapDescription(paris, 'Paris, France');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Open the file in a browser, click the button, and watch the camera glide smoothly to the Eiffel Tower while respecting contrast, hierarchy, and accessibility.

---

## 7. Quick checklist for a production-ready implementation

| ✅ Item | Why it matters |
|--------|----------------|
| **Use `flyTo` (or `easeTo`)** – not manual `setCenter` loops. | Guarantees GPU-accelerated, frame-rate-stable animation. |
| **Set a `duration`** (or let speed/curve compute it) – avoid “instant jump”. | Gives users a mental cue of where they are moving. |
| **Add `essential: true`** – respects reduced-motion preferences. | WCAG 2.1 AA compliance. |
| **Provide a fallback `jumpTo`** when `prefers-reduced-motion` is on. | Prevents motion-sickness. |
| **Keep label halos** (`text-halo-color`, `text-halo-width`) appropriate for the basemap (see the cartography skill). | Guarantees legibility during the flight, especially when the camera tilts. |
| **Update an off-screen description** (`aria-live`) for screen-reader users. | Makes the map navigation perceivable to non-visual users. |
| **Test on both light vector and imagery basemaps** – verify that the halo contrast still meets 4.5:1. | Prevents hidden-label bugs when you switch basemap styles. |
| **Avoid extremely high `pitch` (> 70°)** – label halos become distorted and line-width perception changes. | Maintains visual hierarchy. |
| **Throttle rapid clicks** (e.g., disable the button until the animation ends) or
